NAME
	gbild - GTK+ 2 image viewer

SYNOPSIS
	gbild [-s algorithm] [-S size] [-C colour[:colour]] [-z zoom] [-fpctn] [+fpctnC] [file] ...

DESCRIPTION
	gbild is a GTK+ 2 image viewer.

OPTIONS
	-f	Start in full-screen mode.

	+f	Do not start in full-screen mode.

	-p	Show the property pane.

	+p	Hide the property pane.

	-c	Show the image collection.

	+c	Hide the image collection.

	-t	Apply an image's embedded orientation.

	+t	Do not apply an image's embedded orientation.

	-n	Use the image resolution and display resolution to make
		normal size a physical size.

	+n	Use one source pixel per display pixel for normal size.

	-s algorithm
		Set the scaling algorithm. Supported values are nearest,
		bilinear, and gaussian.

	-S size
		Set the chequer square size in pixels. A size of 0
		disables the chequered background.

	-C colour1[:colour2]
		Enable the chequered background and set its colours.
		If the second colour is omitted, the first colour is used
		for both squares.

		Colours use hexadecimal RGB, RRGGBB, RRRRGGGGBBBB, RGBA,
		RRGGBBAA, or RRRRGGGGBBBBAAAA notation, with an optional
		#, 0x, or 0X prefix. RGB-only forms may have a leading
		alpha percentage; for example, 25%ABCDEF sets alpha to
		25 percent.

	+C	Disable the chequered background.

	-z zoom
		Set the initial zoom. zoom shall either be the zoom
		expressed in perfect (e.g. 100%) or ratio (e.g. 1:1),
		or one of the following modes:

		width
			Fit to width

		height
			Fit to height

		window
			Fit to window

		best
			Best fit

		stretch
			Stretch to window

OPERANDS
	file
		Image file to open.

EXIT STATUS
	0	The program exited successfully.
	1	An error occurred.

SEE ALSO
	None.
